---
// Terms of sale and use. The rules mirror docs/release-and-licensing.md and
// the vocabulary in GLOSSARY.md; change those first, then this page.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Marker from '../components/Marker.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for buying and using Pocket: the License, Activations, the Trial, and who sells it."
>
  <section class="container page">
    <Marker shape="square" play />
    <h1 class="h indent">Terms</h1>
    <div class="indent prose">
    <p class="label muted">Last updated: November 13, 2026</p>

    <p>
      These terms apply when you download, try, buy or use Pocket, a movable, resizable widget
      for the Mac. By using Pocket you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use
      Pocket.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Pocket is made and sold by dk2la, an individual based in France. For any question about
      Pocket or these terms, write to
      <a href="mailto:dk2la@icloud.com">dk2la@icloud.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Orders are handled by Lemon Squeezy, our merchant of record. Lemon Squeezy processes your
      payment, collects any taxes that apply, handles refunds and issues your License key. Its
      own terms apply to the payment itself.
    </p>

    <h2>The Trial</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The Trial lasts 3 days from the first launch of Pocket and includes every feature.</li>
      <li>Starting the Trial needs an internet connection.</li>
      <li>There is one Trial per Mac. Reinstalling Pocket does not restart it.</li>
      <li>
        When the Trial ends and you have no License, Pocket locks until you enter a License key.
        Your settings and data stay intact.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The License</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A License is permanent. You pay once: $24, or $19 while a launch price applies. The
        price shown at checkout is the one you pay.
      </li>
      <li>
        A License includes every future feature of Pocket except Subscription features (see
        below).
      </li>
      <li>
        One License key is for one person. Please don't share, resell or publish it.
      </li>
      <li>
        A License allows up to 3 Activations. An Activation links your License to one Mac. You
        can remove an Activation in Pocket to move it to another Mac.
      </li>
      <li>
        Pocket checks your License key online about once a day. Without a connection it keeps
        working for up to 7 days after the last successful check, then asks you to reconnect.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A License gives you the right to use Pocket. Pocket itself, including its code and
      design, remains the property of dk2la. Don't copy or redistribute it, and don't work
      around the Trial or License checks, except where the law gives you that right.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a License key is shared, published or used to get around these limits, we may disable
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>Subscription features</h2>
    <p>
      We may later add Subscription features: features that need a separate, recurring
      Subscription even if you hold a License. No Subscription exists today. If one is
      introduced, it will be optional and will not remove anything your License already
      includes.
    </p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      You can get a refund within 14 days of purchase if your License key was never activated.
      The details are in the <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what data Pocket and this website
      handle.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates and changes</h2>
    <p>
      We improve Pocket over time, so features may be added, changed or removed. We may also
      update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version. A change to these terms
      does not take away a License you already hold.
    </p>

    <h2>Warranty</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep Pocket reliable, but we provide it as it is. We don't promise that it will
      be free of errors, that it will never be interrupted, or that it will work with every
      version of macOS or every other app. The 3-day Trial is there so you can check that Pocket
